>     Are there any drawbacks to being invisible? 

Yes. People can't see you, for one thing. Neither can monsters, though,
and the Invisible Man figured out a way to deal with this. It depends
on your attitude towards people who can't see you if this is a big
drawback, though.

> How usefull is invisibility
> anyway?

It has specific advantages in combat; monsters will tend not to make
a beeline for you, but wander about a bit trying to find you. Others
will tell you the exact chances, and how much better displacement is.
Note that having monsters _not_ follow you in a beeline makes depositing
a baluchitherium on a _ somewhat more time-consuming.

